## Sources of Truth

1. **Notion** — product rules, architecture, long-term decisions
2. **Figma** — UI only: https://www.figma.com/file/FHbikS2jILAeMv8mote0vD?type=design
3. **GitHub** — code, Issues, PRs, Bugs

## Current phase

Phase 1 = **technical foundation only**.  
Forbidden now: business features, page flows, AI business logic, recipe modules.

## Locked stack

- iOS: Swift 6, SwiftUI, Swift Concurrency, Observation, MVVM, Feature Modules, DI, Protocol-oriented
- UI: Apple iOS 26 Liquid Glass + HIG; native SwiftUI first
- Backend: Supabase (Auth, DB, Storage, Functions)
- Auth: Sign in with Apple + Google → Supabase Auth (never store third-party tokens)
- Pay: StoreKit 2 + RevenueCat (decoupled from business)
- Bundle ID (Phase 1): `com.natefox.cookapp`

## Workflow

Notion → GitHub Issue → Branch → Implement → Test → PR → Review → Merge  
Every code change must link an Issue. Prefer open-source integration over reinventing.
